<AppliedModelCard xmlns="https://mc.chai.org/v0.3/schema.xsd"><Metadata><ModelName /><Developer /><InquiriesOrToReportAnIssue /><ReleaseStage /><ReleaseDate /><Version /><RegulatoryApprovalStatusIfApplicable /><GlobalAvailability /><Summary>Derm Foundation is a machine learning model that generates embeddings for dermatology images, enabling efficient AI model development for dermatology image analysis [SOURCE 1]. It helps businesses and institutions leverage their dermatology data more effectively, needing less data and compute to build AI models [SOURCE 1].</Summary><Keywords /></Metadata><UsesAndDirections><IntendedUseAndWorkflow>Derm Foundation can be used for data-efficient classification tasks like classifying skin conditions, scoring severity, identifying body parts, and determining image quality [SOURCE 1]. The embedding from each skin image only needs to be generated once and can be used as an input for a variety of different classifiers [SOURCE 1].</IntendedUseAndWorkflow><PrimaryIntendedUsers /><NecessaryKnowledgeExpertise /><HowToUse /><TargetedPatientPopulation /><PatientConsentOrDisclosureRequiredOrSuggested /></UsesAndDirections><Warnings><DeveloperSuppliedWarnings /><ModelLimitations>Not specified</ModelLimitations><SkinTypeRepresentationAndEquity /><ClinicalRiskLevel /></Warnings><TrustIngredients><AISystemFacts /><ModelType>Machine learning model [SOURCE 1].</ModelType><InteractionWithOtherSystems /><OutcomesAndOutput /><TypeAndValueOfSolutionOutput /><ExplanationForHowAnOutputIsGenerated /><FoundationModelsUsedInApplicationIfApplicable>Not specified</FoundationModelsUsedInApplicationIfApplicable><InputDataSource /><OutputInputDataType /><DevelopmentDataCharacterization /><TrainingData>Trained on large scale datasets [SOURCE 1].</TrainingData><ExclusionInclusionCriteria /><DemographicRepresentativeness /><DatasetDOIIfApplicable /><DatasetTransparency /><ValidationTestDataset>Not specified</ValidationTestDataset><TimelineOfDataCollection /><SkinTone